# tools/entity-gates-allowlist -- the casts plan_entity.md permits, named by
# file and line.
#
# FORMAT: <path relative to src/>:<line>  [TAB  why]
# Comments start with '#'; blank lines are ignored.
#
# THE DEFINITION OF DONE ALLOWS ONE PER SIDE, AND THAT IS TWO. plan_entity.md's
# clause 3 ends: "The one downcast on an entity path is inside the slot-table
# resolver, which checks the serial before it returns", and §5's gate-3 row says
# that cast "is allowlisted by file and line and covered by the serial-reuse
# test". §3.3 puts ONE TABLE ON EACH SIDE -- "one array per side, owned by the
# side's game-system object" -- and the resolver is per side because the shell
# type is per side: CStandaloneEntity on the server, C_StandaloneEntity on the
# client. So clause 3's "the one downcast" is one per resolver, and there are
# two resolvers. Nothing else belongs here.
#
# A THIRD ENTRY WOULD BE A DIFFERENT KIND OF THING. Both entries below are the
# SAME LINE OF CODE written twice for two types, both sit directly on top of
# CSourceSharpSlotTable::Resolve, and both are covered by a serial-reuse suite
# that goes red when the comparison inside Resolve is deleted. An entry that is
# not that shape is a hole rather than a resolver, and adding one without a
# sentence in plan_entity.md permitting it is how the port ends with three
# downcasts and a green gate.
#
# A STALE ENTRY FAILS GATE 3. Line numbers move when a file is edited, and an
# entry that matches no cast site is no longer excusing the cast it was written
# for -- it is excusing whatever now sits on that line, or nothing at all.
# tools/entity-gates counts entries that matched nothing and fails on them, so
# an edit above the resolver is a red gate, not a silent widening.

sourcesharp/game/server/shell_entityslots.cpp:465	SourceSharp_ShellFromHandle -- §3.3's resolver. The static_cast recovers the concrete shell from the void * the slot table stored at bind time, AFTER CSourceSharpSlotTable::Resolve has compared the serial. Covered by slot_table_test.cpp's SerialReuse cases: deleting the comparison turns six of them red (mutation-verified, step 1c).
sourcesharp/game/client/shell_cliententitylist.cpp:210	SourceSharp_ClientShellFromHandle -- §3.3's resolver, CLIENT arm (Phase 5a). The same line as the server's above, for the client's shell type: static_cast recovers the concrete C_StandaloneEntity from the void * SourceSharp_ClientSlotBindAt stored, AFTER CSourceSharpSlotTable::Resolve has compared the serial. Covered by client_slot_table_test.cpp's ClientSerialReuse and ClientSerialAdoption cases: deleting the comparison turns four of them red (mutation-verified, step 5a).
